---
// D-35 packaging probe — the proposed `exports` map, proven by a build.
//
// The two imports below are the entire test. They are written in exactly the
// shape D-35 specifies for the real package:
//
//     import "@akhil-saxena/design-system/themes/charcoal.css";
//     import "@akhil-saxena/design-system/fonts/charcoal.css";
//
// against a local stub whose package.json carries nothing but the proposed
// map. If this page builds, the map shape resolves. If the wildcard were
// spelled `./themes/*` instead of `./themes/*.css`, the `*` would capture
// `charcoal.css` rather than `charcoal`, the target would substitute to
// `themes/charcoal.css.css`, and the build would fail — which is not a
// hypothetical, it is the live defect in the design system's existing
// per-component CSS entry, filed as G-12.
//
// WHY A STUB AND NOT THE REAL PACKAGE. `../design-system` is not throwaway and
// Phase 0 has no authority to change it: adding these entries also means
// extending `files` and the hard-coded copy loop in `scripts/postbuild.mjs`,
// which is Phase 1's work in a repo with its own tests and release process.
// The alternative — leaving the shape unverified until then — is how a spec
// ships wrong. See fixtures/stub-theme-pkg/README.md.
//
// WHY `import.meta.resolve()` WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN ENOUGH. It performs pattern
// substitution and hands back a URL without ever stat-ing the target, so it
// reports the broken spelling as resolvable while the build fails on it. Only
// a build is authoritative here, which is why this is a page and not a script.
//
// No hydration directive: this route ships zero framework JS and stays inside
// check-no-js.sh's protection rather than its exclusion list.

import "stub-theme-pkg/themes/charcoal.css";
import "stub-theme-pkg/fonts/charcoal.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-brand="charcoal">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>probe/exports — D-35 exports-map shape</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>D-35 exports map</h1>
		<p>
			Two subpaths resolved from a stub package carrying only the proposed map:
			<code>themes/charcoal.css</code> and <code>fonts/charcoal.css</code>. The wildcard is
			spelled with the extension — <code>./themes/*.css</code>, not <code>./themes/*</code>
			— which is what makes the specifier D-35 names resolve instead of doubling its
			suffix.
		</p>
		<p>
			If this page built, the shape is proven. That is the whole assertion; nothing here
			reads a token value.
		</p>
	</body>
</html>
